# solar: run a SteamVR session while the PS VR2 headset is powered on
# (freender/homelab-ops#389). The Linux side of void's "PS VR2 Audio" Task
# Scheduler trigger: the headset's USB audio card appears behind the passed-through
# xHCI, and the logged-in user's systemd manager starts psvr2-steamvr.service.
# The /dev/psvr2 alias (dev-psvr2.device) is what that unit binds to, so the card
# disappearing on headset power-off stops it. Not limited to "add": a change event
# that dropped the alias would stop the unit. 054c:0cde is the PS VR2 headset.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="card*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="054c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0cde", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_ALIAS}+="/dev/psvr2", ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}+="psvr2-steamvr.service"
